          "content": {
            "size": 0,
            "compression": 0,
            "mimeType": "x-unknown",
            "text": "[{\"analysisId\":515,\"transcriptId\":406,\"callDate\":\"2026-05-06T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Disney (DIS) Q2 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":400,\"symbol\":\"DIS\",\"shortName\":\"Disney\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":null,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (credibility flipped to negative this quarter) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":502,\"transcriptId\":393,\"callDate\":\"2026-05-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"AMD (AMD) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":111,\"symbol\":\"AMD\",\"shortName\":\"AMD\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":42,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst has shown two quarters of soft signals (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) — typically this would prompt the trend layer to step the recommendation down one notch. But the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening, which means the position is fundamentally working. On rising-conviction calls, mild soft signals usually reflect the analyst sizing the position more disciplinedly rather than the thesis breaking. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but keeps the per-call rec in place.\"},{\"analysisId\":518,\"transcriptId\":409,\"callDate\":\"2026-05-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"PayPal (PYPL) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":403,\"symbol\":\"PYPL\",\"shortName\":\"PayPal\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Weakening\",\"recommendedSize\":15,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The analyst has already flagged the thesis as Weakening on this call, which is a more decisive signal than anything the trend layer would add. The downstream allocator's graduated exit ratchet (trim → trim more → exit over successive quarters of non-improvement) takes over from here, so the trend layer doesn't issue a separate override — it just confirms the deteriorating direction.\"},{\"analysisId\":516,\"transcriptId\":407,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Mastercard (MA) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":401,\"symbol\":\"MA\",\"shortName\":\"Mastercard\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst has shown two quarters of soft signals (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) — typically this would prompt the trend layer to step the recommendation down one notch. But the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening, which means the position is fundamentally working. On rising-conviction calls, mild soft signals usually reflect the analyst sizing the position more disciplinedly rather than the thesis breaking. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but keeps the per-call rec in place.\"},{\"analysisId\":507,\"transcriptId\":398,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-29T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Meta (META) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":392,\"symbol\":\"META\",\"shortName\":\"Meta\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":55,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst stepped conviction up this quarter (higher recommended size, fresh-money gap not widening, no credibility or mitigation concerns). On an established ticker we wait for a second confirming quarter before stepping the recommendation up — one strong quarter on a mature name can be noise. Watch this; if next quarter also comes in improving, the trend layer will upgrade.\"},{\"analysisId\":254,\"transcriptId\":145,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-29T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Alphabet (GOOGL) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":106,\"symbol\":\"GOOGL\",\"shortName\":\"Alphabet\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":55,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":245,\"transcriptId\":136,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-29T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Microsoft (MSFT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":82,\"symbol\":\"MSFT\",\"shortName\":\"Microsoft\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":18,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":503,\"transcriptId\":394,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-28T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Enphase Energy (ENPH) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":65,\"symbol\":\"ENPH\",\"shortName\":\"Enphase Energy\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Weakening\",\"recommendedSize\":25,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The analyst has already flagged the thesis as Weakening on this call, which is a more decisive signal than anything the trend layer would add. The downstream allocator's graduated exit ratchet (trim → trim more → exit over successive quarters of non-improvement) takes over from here, so the trend layer doesn't issue a separate override — it just confirms the deteriorating direction.\"},{\"analysisId\":244,\"transcriptId\":135,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-22T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Tesla (TSLA) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":35,\"symbol\":\"TSLA\",\"shortName\":\"Tesla\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":520,\"transcriptId\":411,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-16T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Netflix (NFLX) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":390,\"symbol\":\"NFLX\",\"shortName\":\"Netflix\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":513,\"transcriptId\":404,\"callDate\":\"2026-04-14T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Johnson & Johnson (JNJ) Q1 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":398,\"symbol\":\"JNJ\",\"shortName\":\"Johnson & Johnson\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":8,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":501,\"transcriptId\":392,\"callDate\":\"2026-03-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amprius (AMPX) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":6,\"symbol\":\"AMPX\",\"shortName\":\"Amprius\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":28,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for a trim, but the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening and none of the harder warning signs (credibility break, mitigation track record erosion) have fired. On a Strengthening thesis, a soft-only streak usually reflects the analyst getting more disciplined on a winning name — sizing it more carefully — rather than the thesis itself deteriorating. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but doesn't override the per-call recommendation.\"},{\"analysisId\":119,\"transcriptId\":18,\"callDate\":\"2026-03-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amprius (AMPX) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":6,\"symbol\":\"AMPX\",\"shortName\":\"Amprius\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for a trim, but the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening and none of the harder warning signs (credibility break, mitigation track record erosion) have fired. On a Strengthening thesis, a soft-only streak usually reflects the analyst getting more disciplined on a winning name — sizing it more carefully — rather than the thesis itself deteriorating. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but doesn't override the per-call recommendation.\"},{\"analysisId\":141,\"transcriptId\":25,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-26T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Eos Energy (EOSE) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":12,\"symbol\":\"EOSE\",\"shortName\":\"Eos\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":20,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and credibility flipped to negative this quarter) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":170,\"transcriptId\":101,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-26T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Sunrun (RUN) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":95,\"symbol\":\"RUN\",\"shortName\":\"Sunrun\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":135,\"transcriptId\":86,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-25T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Enovix (ENVX) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":74,\"symbol\":\"ENVX\",\"shortName\":\"Enovix\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":28,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"flattening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"The thesis just stepped down from Strengthening to Intact, with none of the soft warning signs firing — typical of a growth name maturing into a steady-state cash generator. It's not deteriorating, but the upside is no longer compounding the way it was. The trend layer doesn't automatically act on this: the right call depends on whether there's a higher-conviction candidate to rotate into, which is a Layer 3 (opportunity scanner) decision we haven't built yet. Until then, treat this as a 'on deck for review' signal.\"},{\"analysisId\":255,\"transcriptId\":146,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-25T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"NVIDIA (NVDA) Q4 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":58,\"symbol\":\"NVDA\",\"shortName\":\"NVIDIA\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":146,\"transcriptId\":94,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-24T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"First Solar (FSLR) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":88,\"symbol\":\"FSLR\",\"shortName\":\"First Solar\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":25,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The previous quarter showed soft signals (analyst getting more cautious), and this quarter the picture got worse — two or more concerns fired at once (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the mitigation track record (whether management has historically delivered on this kind of headwind) got weaker). At least one of those is a hard signal (credibility breaking down or mitigation track record eroding), which means the deterioration isn't just noise. The trend layer overrides to a trim regardless of what the per-call rec says.\"},{\"analysisId\":510,\"transcriptId\":401,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-19T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Walmart (WMT) Q4 2026 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":395,\"symbol\":\"WMT\",\"shortName\":\"Walmart\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":47,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":253,\"transcriptId\":144,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"AMD (AMD) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":111,\"symbol\":\"AMD\",\"shortName\":\"AMD\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":379,\"transcriptId\":270,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Enphase Energy (ENPH) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":65,\"symbol\":\"ENPH\",\"shortName\":\"Enphase Energy\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":null,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"flattening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"The thesis just stepped down from Strengthening to Intact, with none of the soft warning signs firing — typical of a growth name maturing into a steady-state cash generator. It's not deteriorating, but the upside is no longer compounding the way it was. The trend layer doesn't automatically act on this: the right call depends on whether there's a higher-conviction candidate to rotate into, which is a Layer 3 (opportunity scanner) decision we haven't built yet. Until then, treat this as a 'on deck for review' signal.\"},{\"analysisId\":523,\"transcriptId\":414,\"callDate\":\"2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"PayPal (PYPL) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":403,\"symbol\":\"PYPL\",\"shortName\":\"PayPal\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Weakening\",\"recommendedSize\":15,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The analyst has already flagged the thesis as Weakening on this call, which is a more decisive signal than anything the trend layer would add. The downstream allocator's graduated exit ratchet (trim → trim more → exit over successive quarters of non-improvement) takes over from here, so the trend layer doesn't issue a separate override — it just confirms the deteriorating direction.\"},{\"analysisId\":525,\"transcriptId\":416,\"callDate\":\"2026-01-29T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Mastercard (MA) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":401,\"symbol\":\"MA\",\"shortName\":\"Mastercard\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":534,\"transcriptId\":425,\"callDate\":\"2026-01-28T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Meta (META) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":392,\"symbol\":\"META\",\"shortName\":\"Meta\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":52,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":183,\"transcriptId\":47,\"callDate\":\"2026-01-28T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Tesla (TSLA) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":35,\"symbol\":\"TSLA\",\"shortName\":\"Tesla\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":55,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst stepped conviction up this quarter (higher recommended size, fresh-money gap not widening, no credibility or mitigation concerns). On an established ticker we wait for a second confirming quarter before stepping the recommendation up — one strong quarter on a mature name can be noise. Watch this; if next quarter also comes in improving, the trend layer will upgrade.\"},{\"analysisId\":527,\"transcriptId\":418,\"callDate\":\"2026-01-27T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"UnitedHealth (UNH) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":399,\"symbol\