gthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst stepped conviction up this quarter (higher recommended size, fresh-money gap not widening, no credibility or mitigation concerns). On a speculative ticker (small-cap, volatile, or pre-revenue), waiting for a second confirming quarter often means missing the inflection — these names move fast. The trend layer steps the recommendation up one notch now (Hold → Add) rather than waiting.\"},{\"analysisId\":529,\"transcriptId\":420,\"callDate\":\"2026-01-13T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"JPMorgan Chase (JPM) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":396,\"symbol\":\"JPM\",\"shortName\":\"JPMorgan Chase\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":null,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"flattening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"The thesis just stepped down from Strengthening to Intact, with none of the soft warning signs firing — typical of a growth name maturing into a steady-state cash generator. It's not deteriorating, but the upside is no longer compounding the way it was. The trend layer doesn't automatically act on this: the right call depends on whether there's a higher-conviction candidate to rotate into, which is a Layer 3 (opportunity scanner) decision we haven't built yet. Until then, treat this as a 'on deck for review' signal.\"},{\"analysisId\":533,\"transcriptId\":424,\"callDate\":\"2025-12-10T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Adobe (ADBE) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":393,\"symbol\":\"ADBE\",\"shortName\":\"Adobe\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage p