s it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":218,\"transcriptId\":117,\"callDate\":\"2025-11-04T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"AMD (AMD) Q3 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":111,\"symbol\":\"AMD\",\"shortName\":\"AMD\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":55,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst stepped conviction up this quarter (higher recommended size, fresh-money gap not widening, no credibility or mitigation concerns). On a speculative ticker (small-cap, volatile, or pre-revenue), waiting for a second confirming quarter often means missing the inflection — these names move fast. The trend layer steps the recommendation up one notch now (Hold → Add) rather than waiting.\"},{\"analysisId\":536,\"transcriptId\":427,\"callDate\":\"2025-10-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amazon (AMZN) Q3 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":391,\"symbol\":\"AMZN\",\"shortName\":\"Amazon\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":52,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for a trim, but the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening and none of the harder warning signs (credibility break, mitigation track record erosion) have fired. On a Strengthening thesis, a soft-only streak usually reflects the analyst getting more disciplined on a winning name — sizing it more carefully — rather than the thesis itself deteriorating. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but doesn't override the per-call recommendation.\"},{\"analysisId\":112,\"transcriptId\":55,\"callDate\":\"2025-10-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Apple (AAPL) Q4 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":43,\"symbol\":\"AAPL\",\"shortName\":\"Apple\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":145,\"transcriptId\":96,\"callDate\":\"2025-10-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"First Solar (FSLR) Q3 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":88,\"symbol\":\"FSLR\",\"shortName\":\"First Solar\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":28,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysi