jectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The analyst has already flagged the thesis as Weakening on this call, which is a more decisive signal than anything the trend layer would add. The downstream allocator's graduated exit ratchet (trim → trim more → exit over successive quarters of non-improvement) takes over from here, so the trend layer doesn't issue a separate override — it just confirms the deteriorating direction.\"},{\"analysisId\":180,\"transcriptId\":48,\"callDate\":\"2025-04-22T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Tesla (TSLA) Q1 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":35,\"symbol\":\"TSLA\",\"shortName\":\"Tesla\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying); credibility flipped to negative this quarter; and the mitigation track record (whether management has historically delivered on this kind of headwind) got weaker) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":581,\"transcriptId\":472,\"callDate\":\"2025-04-17T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Netflix (NFLX) Q1 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":390,\"symbol\":\"NFLX\",\"shortName\":\"Netflix\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recomme