 prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":276,\"transcriptId\":167,\"callDate\":\"2025-03-20T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amprius (AMPX) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":6,\"symbol\":\"AMPX\",\"shortName\":\"Amprius\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"flattening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The thesis just stepped down from Strengthening to Intact, with none of the soft warning signs firing — typical of a growth name maturing into a steady-state cash generator. It's not deteriorating, but the upside is no longer compounding the way it was. The trend layer doesn't automatically act on this: the right call depends on whether there's a higher-conviction candidate to rotate into, which is a Layer 3 (opportunity scanner) decision we haven't built yet. Until then, treat this as a 'on deck for review' signal.\"},{\"analysisId\":569,\"transcriptId\":460,\"callDate\":\"2025-03-12T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Adobe (ADBE) Q1 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":393,\"symbol\":\"ADBE\",\"shortName\":\"Adobe\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":35,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst has shown two quarters of soft signals (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) — typically this would prompt the trend layer to step the recommendation down one notch. But the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening, which means 