ation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":137,\"transcriptId\":21,\"callDate\":\"2025-03-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Eos Energy (EOSE) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":12,\"symbol\":\"EOSE\",\"shortName\":\"Eos\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":35,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"Two quarters in a row of strengthening conviction — the analyst keeps raising recommended size while keeping the fresh-money gap tight, with no credibility or mitigation concerns appearing. That's a clean inflection signal across multiple periods, not a one-off. The trend layer steps the recommendation up one notch (Hold → Add).\"},{\"analysisId\":142,\"transcriptId\":100,\"callDate\":\"2025-02-25T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"First Solar (FSLR) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":88,\"symbol\":\"FSLR\",\"shortName\":\"First Solar\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Weakening\",\"recommendedSize\":25,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The analyst has already flagged the thesis as Weakening on this call, which is a more decisive signal than anything the trend layer would add. The downstream allocator's graduated exit ratchet (trim → trim more → exit over successive quarters of non-improvement) takes over from here, so the trend layer doesn't issue a separate override — it just confirms the deteriorating direction.\"},{\"analysisId\":131,\"transcriptId\":82,\"callDate\":\"2025-02-19T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Enovix (ENVX) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":74,\"symbol\":\"ENVX\",\"shortName\":\"Enovix\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\