            "mimeType": "x-unknown",
            "text": "[{\"id\":43,\"symbol\":\"AAPL\",\"name\":\"Apple Inc.\",\"shortName\":\"Apple\",\"status\":\"portfolio\",\"capPercent\":35,\"type\":\"A\",\"transcriptCount\":22,\"lastCallDate\":\"2026-04-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"daysSinceLastCall\":30,\"latestAnalysis\":{\"id\":252,\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendation\":\"Add\",\"recommendedSize\":52,\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-02T15:51:26.910Z\",\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"stable\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"finalConfidence\":\"confident\",\"trendRationale\":\"Recent quarters look broadly consistent — conviction holding, no soft signals firing, no improving inflection either. Nothing for the trend layer to act on; the per-call recommendation passes through unchanged.\"}},{\"id\":393,\"symbol\":\"ADBE\",\"name\":\"Adobe Inc.\",\"shortName\":\"Adobe\",\"status\":\"watchlist\",\"capPercent\":35,\"type\":\"A\",\"transcriptCount\":21,\"lastCallDate\":\"2026-03-12T00:00:00.000Z\",\"daysSinceLastCall\":79,\"latestAnalysis\":{\"id\":508,\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendation\":\"Add\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-10T16:07:11.791Z\",\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"stable\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"finalConfidence\":\"confident\",\"trendRationale\":\"Recent quarters look broadly consistent — conviction holding, no soft signals firing, no improving inflection either. Nothing for the trend layer to act on; the per-call recommendation passes through unchanged.\"}},{\"id\":111,\"symbol\":\"AMD\",\"name\":\"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.\",\"shortName\":\"AMD\",\"status\":\"watchlist\",\"capPercent\":35,\"type\":\"A\",\"transcriptCount\":21,\"lastCallDate\":\"2026-05-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"daysSinceLastCall\":25,\"latestAnalysis\":{\"id\":502,\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendation\":\"Add\",\"recommendedSize\":42,\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-07T15:26:11.360Z\",\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"finalConfidence\":\"advisory\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst has shown two quarters of soft signals (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) — typically this would prompt the trend layer to step the recommendation down one notch. But the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening, which means the position is fundamentally working. On rising-conviction calls, mild soft signals usually reflect the analyst sizing the position more disciplinedly rather than the thesis breaking. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but keeps the per-call rec in place.\"}},{\"id\":6,\"symbol\":\"AMPX\",\"name\":\"Amprius Technologies, Inc.\",\"shortName\":\"Amprius\",\"status\":\"portfolio\",\"capPercent\":35,\"type\":\"A\",\"transcriptCount\":14,\"lastCallDate\":\"2026-03-05T00:00:00.000Z\",\"daysSinceLastCall\":86,\"latestAnalysis\":{\"id\":119,\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendation\":\"Add\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"createdAt\":\"2026-04-26T21:49:01.016Z\",\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"finalConfidence\":\"advisory\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for a trim, but the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening and none of the harder warning signs (credibility break, mitigation track record erosion) have fired. On a Strengthening thesis, a soft-only streak usually reflects the analyst getting more disciplined on a winning name — sizing it more carefully — rather than the thesis itself deteriorating. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but doesn't override