"established\",\"trajectory\":\"stable\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"finalConfidence\":\"confident\",\"trendRationale\":\"Recent quarters look broadly consistent — conviction holding, no soft signals firing, no improving inflection either. Nothing for the trend layer to act on; the per-call recommendation passes through unchanged.\"}},{\"id\":400,\"symbol\":\"DIS\",\"name\":\"The Walt Disney Company\",\"shortName\":\"Disney\",\"status\":\"watchlist\",\"capPercent\":35,\"type\":\"A\",\"transcriptCount\":22,\"lastCallDate\":\"2026-05-06T00:00:00.000Z\",\"daysSinceLastCall\":24,\"latestAnalysis\":{\"id\":515,\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendation\":\"Hold\",\"recommendedSize\":null,\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-10T16:14:26.490Z\",\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"finalConfidence\":\"advisory\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (credibility flipped to negative this quarter) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"}},{\"id\":65,\"symbol\":\"ENPH\",\"name\":\"Enphase Energy, Inc.\",\"shortName\":\"Enphase Energy\",\"status\":\"watchlist\",\"capPercent\":35,\"type\":\"A\",\"transcriptCount\":21,\"lastCallDate\":\"2026-04-28T00:00:00.000Z\",\"daysSinceLastCall\":32,\"latestAnalysis\":{\"id\":503,\"thesisHealth\":\"Weakening\",\"recommendation\":\"Trim\",\"recommendedSize\":25,\"createdAt\":\"2026-05-07T15:28:37.169Z\",\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"suggestedOverride\":null,\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"finalConfidence\":\"advisory\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-g